{% doc %}
  The import channel of a product, decided in this one place so the product page can't call a
  product "יבואן רשמי" in one spot and something else in another. snippets/product-specs (the
  warranty row), snippets/product-trust (the warranty line and trust point) and snippets/badges
  (the channel badge of the product page) print what this returns; none of them reads the
  channel tags or the warranty metafields on its own.

  Precedence, first match wins:
  1. Tags (exact): "יד שניה" or "יד שנייה" → used, "מחודש" → refurbished, "מקביל" → parallel.
     Such a product is never official, whatever the metafields or the title say.
  2. Metafields: custom.warranty_channel naming "מקביל" → parallel; custom.warranty_official
     true → official; custom.warranty_channel naming "יבואן רשמי" → official; any other
     custom.warranty_channel text (a warranty provider such as "DCS") → other.
  3. Nothing: the channel is unknown and nothing is printed.
  Not sources, on purpose: the title suffix (" – יבואן רשמי", written by the POS import; on
  some products it contradicts the tags) and the tag "רשמי". "Official" is only ever the
  owner's explicit metafield.

  Label (default output), the words after the warranty months:
  - from a tag: "יבוא מקביל" for parallel (used and refurbished already say so in the title and
    the schema itemCondition), then the custom.warranty_channel text when it names a warranty
    provider and not an import channel (no "יבוא" in it): "יבוא מקביל · DCS".
  - from the metafields: the custom.warranty_channel text, else "יבואן רשמי" when
    custom.warranty_official is true (the rule product-specs and product-trust had before).

  @param {product} product - The product.
  @param {string} [format] - 'label' (default) or 'key': official | parallel | used | refurbished | other, or nothing.

  @example
  {%- capture channel_label -%}{%- render 'import-channel', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture channel_key -%}{%- render 'import-channel', product: product, format: 'key' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign ic_text = product.metafields.custom.warranty_channel.value | strip
  assign ic_official = product.metafields.custom.warranty_official.value

  assign ic_key = ''
  assign ic_from_tag = true
  if product.tags contains 'יד שניה' or product.tags contains 'יד שנייה'
    assign ic_key = 'used'
  elsif product.tags contains 'מחודש'
    assign ic_key = 'refurbished'
  elsif product.tags contains 'מקביל'
    assign ic_key = 'parallel'
  else
    assign ic_from_tag = false
    if ic_text contains 'מקביל'
      assign ic_key = 'parallel'
    elsif ic_official == true
      assign ic_key = 'official'
    elsif ic_text contains 'יבואן רשמי'
      assign ic_key = 'official'
    elsif ic_text != blank
      assign ic_key = 'other'
    endif
  endif

  if format == 'key'
    echo ic_key
  else
    assign ic_label = ''
    if ic_from_tag
      if ic_key == 'parallel'
        assign ic_label = 'products.product.import_parallel' | t
      endif
      # A provider ("DCS") is kept; a text that names an import channel would contradict the tag.
      if ic_text != blank
        unless ic_text contains 'יבוא'
          if ic_label != blank
            assign ic_label = ic_label | append: ' · '
          endif
          assign ic_label = ic_label | append: ic_text
        endunless
      endif
    else
      assign ic_label = ic_text
      if ic_label == blank and ic_key == 'official'
        assign ic_label = 'products.product.warranty_official' | t
      endif
    endif
    echo ic_label
  endif
-%}
